      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean, i don't have a headache or anything, everything feels back to normal now. but i've heard people say that these \"one-time things\" are actually warnings for a bigger stroke later on. if i decide to just stay home and monitor it like you're saying, what should i actually be looking for to know if it's getting dangerous? i don't want to end up in the hospital for no reason if it's just a vasospasm.",
